turnip/kgsl: highest GPU clock while the user interacts

KGSL's governor keeps a nested desktop's frames at the lowest clock: the
GPU is about 60% busy there, too little to ramp up, and frames miss the
120 Hz vsync (a desktop drag ran at 74 fps instead of 107). DroidNux's
compositor moves the mtime of /tmp/.droidnux-gpu-boost a second past the
user's latest input; until then each queue sets KGSL's per-context power
constraint to the highest level, and drops it afterwards. Boosting all the
time cost 46% more power on a page animating by itself.

